      <title>Go Daily Question 036</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_036/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:44:12 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_036/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Will the following code compile? If so, what will be the output?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func GetValue() int {&#xA;    return 1&#xA;}&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    i := GetValue()&#xA;    switch i.(type) {&#xA;    case int:&#xA;        println(&amp;#34;int&amp;#34;)&#xA;    case string:&#xA;        println(&amp;#34;string&amp;#34;)&#xA;    case interface{}:&#xA;        println(&amp;#34;interface&amp;#34;)&#xA;    default:&#xA;        println(&amp;#34;unknown&amp;#34;)&#xA;    }&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;Answer: Compilation error.&#xA;Type assertion is used here. However, note that only interface types can perform type assertion. &lt;code&gt;i.(type)&lt;/code&gt; is used here, but the type of &lt;code&gt;i&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;int&lt;/code&gt;, not an interface.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
